          "date": "2026-11-25 08:51:48.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-16960 build: loosen kmod-osd and osd-mount version Requires",
        "message": "LU-16960 build: loosen kmod-osd and osd-mount version Requires\n\nkmod-lustre-osd-* required osd-*-mount of exactly the same version,\nand lustre-osd-{zfs,wbcfs}-mount required lustre-osd-* of exactly\nthe same version.  Installing a newer Lustre for a newly installed\nkernel next to the build for the running kernel, before rebooting,\nwould fail when upgrading the userspace packages:\n\n  lustre-osd-ldiskfs-mount = 2.17.61 is needed by (installed)\n  kmod-lustre-osd-ldiskfs\n\nRequire only the same major.minor version in both directions, as\nlustre already does for kmod-lustre.  The new kmods can then be\ninstalled beside the old ones with \"rpm -i\" and the userspace\npackages upgraded with \"rpm -U\".\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Ibe89c1e36281c7b1474b0dc07bdf538e153ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
